let __v_84 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Octopuses have three hearts and blue blood. Two hearts pump to the gills and one to the rest of the body, and the blood is blue because it carries oxygen on copper.\",\"Sharks are older than trees. Sharks have been around about 450 million years, trees about 385 million.\",\"A day on Venus is longer than its year: it turns once every 243 Earth days and goes round the sun in 225.\",\"Bananas are berries and strawberries are not. Botanically a berry has its seeds inside, which a banana does and a strawberry, with its seeds on the outside, does not.\",\"Wombats do cube-shaped droppings, and the corners come from the shape of the last bit of their gut.\",\"A group of flamingos is called a flamboyance.\",\"The Eiffel Tower is about 15cm taller in summer, because the iron expands in the heat.\",\"A hummingbird's heart can beat more than 1,000 times a minute, and it can go into a sleep-like torpor at night to save energy.\",\"Sea otters hold hands while they sleep so they do not drift apart.\",\"The Moon moves about 3.8cm further away from the Earth every year. You can measure it with the mirrors the Apollo crews left behind.\",\"Honey does not go off: it is too sugary and too acidic for bacteria to grow in, so a sealed jar keeps for years - and pots from Egyptian tombs have been found still edible.\",\"Your body makes about a litre and a half of saliva a day, which is most of what you swallow.\",\"There are more possible games of chess than there are atoms in the observable universe, which is why nobody has solved it.\",\"A teaspoon of neutron star would weigh billions of tonnes on Earth, because the matter in it is packed as tightly as an atomic nucleus.\",\"Snails have thousands of teeth, arranged in rows on a ribbon called a radula, and they use them like a file.\"]}")?;
