let __v_85 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Which planet is tipped so far over that it rolls round the sun on its side? (Uranus - it is tilted about 98 degrees.) Ask for another whenever you like.\",\"Which is the largest ocean on Earth? (The Pacific - it covers about a third of the planet.)\",\"How many bones are there in an adult human body? (206 - a baby is born with about 300, and many of them fuse together.)\",\"What is the chemical symbol for gold? (Au, from the Latin aurum. Silver is Ag, from argentum.)\",\"Which is the only mammal that can truly fly? (The bat. A flying squirrel only glides.)\",\"What is the capital of Australia? (Canberra - not Sydney or Melbourne.) Another one is one word away.\",\"How long does sunlight take to reach the Earth? (About 8 minutes 20 seconds, so you always see the sun as it was eight minutes ago.)\",\"Which language has the most native speakers in the world? (Mandarin Chinese, with roughly 940 million.)\",\"What is the smallest country in the world? (Vatican City, about 0.44 square kilometres.)\",\"Who wrote Romeo and Juliet? (William Shakespeare, around 1595.)\",\"What is the hardest natural substance on Earth? (Diamond - a 10 on the Mohs scale, with corundum, the stuff of rubies and sapphires, down at 9.)\",\"How many players from one side are on the pitch in a football match? (Eleven, goalkeeper included.)\",\"At what temperature does water boil at sea level? (100°C. On a mountain it boils lower, because there is less air pressing on it.)\",\"What gas do plants take out of the air to grow? (Carbon dioxide - they keep the carbon and give the oxygen back.)\",\"How many strings does a standard guitar have? (Six.)\",\"In which year did people first walk on the Moon? (1969 - Apollo 11, in July.)\",\"Which is the biggest planet in our solar system? (Jupiter - it is more than twice as heavy as all the other planets put together.)\",\"Which is longer, a mile or a kilometre? (A mile: about 1.6 kilometres, which is why a 5k run is a bit over three miles.)\",\"What is the tallest animal in the world? (The giraffe, up to about 5.5 metres.)\",\"How many sides does a hexagon have? (Six.) Ask for another if you fancy a harder one.\",\"What is the currency of Japan? (The yen.)\",\"Which sea has no coast? (The Sargasso Sea, in the middle of the Atlantic: it is held together by currents rather than by land.)\"]}")?;
