let __v_86 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"dogs\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"dog\",\"dogs\",\"puppy\",\"puppies\",\"pup\",\"pups\",\"doggy\",\"doggo\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"A dog has about 300 million smell receptors in its nose, roughly forty times what a person has, which is why a walk is mostly reading.\",\"A dog's nose print is as individual as a fingerprint, and the wetness helps it work out which direction a smell came from.\"]}]}],[\"cats\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cat\",\"cats\",\"kitten\",\"kittens\",\"kitty\",\"moggy\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"A cat has about thirty muscles in each ear and can turn them most of the way round, and it spends two thirds of its life asleep - up to sixteen hours a day.\",\"A cat's purr runs at 25 to 150 vibrations a second, and cats also purr when they are hurt or frightened, not only when they are content.\"]}]}],[\"bees\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"bee\",\"bees\",\"honeybee\",\"honeybees\",\"bumblebee\",\"bumblebees\",\"bumble bee\",\"bumble bees\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"A honeybee that finds food comes back and dances: a wiggle run straight up the comb means fly towards the sun, and how long she wiggles says how far.\",\"One worker bee makes about a twelfth of a teaspoon of honey in her whole life, which is why a jar is a lot of flying.\"]}]}],[\"elephants\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"elephant\",\"elephants\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Elephants talk in rumbles mostly too low for us to hear, and a herd can pick one up from several kilometres away through the ground as well as the air.\",\"An elephant's trunk has around 40,000 muscles in it and no bones at all, which is how it can pick up a single blade of grass and then lift a tree.\"]}]}],[\"spiders\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"spider\",\"spiders\",\"tarantula\",\"tarantulas\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"A spider feels its web rather than sees it: one strand tells it the size of what landed and whether it is still struggling.\",\"Spider silk is stronger than steel for its weight and can stretch about four times its length before it breaks.\"]}]}],[\"birds\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"bird\",\"birds\",\"sparrow\",\"sparrows\",\"robin\",\"robins\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"A bird's lungs fill in one direction only, with air sacs behind it, which is how a bar-tailed godwit flew 12,000 km without stopping.\",\"Most small birds weigh less than the batteries in a television remote, and a blue tit eats close to its own body weight in food every day in winter.\"]}]}],[\"whales\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"whale\",\"whales\",\"dolphin\",\"dolphins\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"A blue whale's heart is about the size of a small car and slows to two beats a minute when it dives, and its call carries hundreds of kilometres through water.\",\"Dolphins sleep one half of the brain at a time, keeping the other half and one eye on watch so they remember to breathe.\"]}]}],[\"penguins\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"penguin\",\"penguins\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Penguins cannot taste sweetness - the gene for it is broken in them - and they can drink sea water because a gland above the eye filters the salt out.\",\"A penguin's knees and thighs are inside its body, which is why it looks like it has none and why it waddles instead of striding.\"]}]}],[\"butterflies\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"butterfly\",\"butterflies\",\"moth\",\"moths\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Butterflies taste with their feet, and they cannot fly once their body drops below about 15C, which is why they sit with their wings open in the sun.\",\"A caterpillar turns almost all of itself into soup inside the chrysalis and rebuilds from the same cells, so the butterfly is not the caterpillar with wings on.\"]}]}],[\"trees\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tree\",\"trees\",\"oak\",\"oaks\",\"forest\",\"forests\",\"woodland\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Trees pass sugar to each other through fungi in the soil: a beech can feed a shaded seedling of its own kind through that network.\",\"A big oak can pull hundreds of litres of water a day up its trunk, and the tallest trees are limited by how high water can be lifted, not by how strong the wood is.\"]}]}],[\"rain\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"rain\",\"raining\",\"rainy\",\"weather\",\"thunder\",\"thunderstorm\",\"lightning\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"The smell after rain is not the rain: it is geosmin, made by soil bacteria, and a human nose can pick it out at a few parts per trillion.\",\"Lightning heats the air around it to about 30,000C, five times the surface of the sun, and the bang is that air expanding at once.\"]}]}],[\"sleep\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sleep\",\"sleeping\",\"insomnia\",\"dream\",\"dreams\",\"dreaming\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"After about seventeen hours awake, people perform about as badly as someone at the drink-drive limit, which is why a late night feels like a hangover.\",\"The brain flushes waste out of itself mostly while you sleep, using a channel that opens up in deep sleep and barely runs when you are awake.\"]}]}],[\"coffee\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"coffee\",\"caffeine\",\"espresso\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Caffeine does not give you energy: it blocks the receptor that tells you you are tired, so the tiredness piles up behind it and lands when the coffee wears off.\",\"Coffee was chewed, not drunk, for centuries before anyone thought to brew it, and the plant is a fruit stone: the bean is the seed of a cherry.\"]}]}],[\"chocolate\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chocolate\",\"cocoa\",\"cacao\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Chocolate was drunk for most of its history - the Aztecs took it cold, bitter and spiced with chilli - and milk chocolate only arrived in 1875.\",\"Cocoa trees grow in the shade of taller ones, and a tree takes four or five years before it makes a pod worth picking.\"]}]}],[\"cheese\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cheese\",\"cheddar\",\"brie\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Cheese is the same few ingredients with different bacteria, and much of the flavour is made at the rind: a washed rind is wiped with brine so the smellier bacteria win.\",\"Hard cheese keeps for months because most of the water has been pressed and salted out of it, which is what stops the mould that would spoil milk.\"]}]}],[\"brain\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"brain\",\"brains\",\"memory\",\"memories\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Your brain is about two per cent of your weight and uses about a fifth of your energy, and it has no pain receptors of its own - a headache comes from the layers and vessels around it.\",\"A memory is not stored in one place: remembering something re-runs the same pattern across the brain, which is why a memory changes a little each time you recall it.\"]}]}],[\"sun\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sun\",\"sunlight\",\"sunshine\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"The sunlight on your arm is old: the energy took tens of thousands of years to work its way out of the sun's core, and then eight minutes to cross to you.\",\"The sun is 99.8 per cent of the mass of the solar system - everything else, planets included, is the leftover dust.\"]}]}],[\"sea\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sea\",\"ocean\",\"oceans\",\"seabed\",\"sea bed\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"We have better maps of Mars than of the sea floor: about three quarters of it has never been surveyed in detail, and the deepest trench would swallow Everest with two kilometres to spare.\",\"The sea is salty because rain has been washing rock into it for billions of years, and the water that leaves by evaporation takes none of the salt with it.\"]}]}],[\"space\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"space\",\"universe\",\"galaxy\",\"galaxies\",\"star\",\"stars\",\"planet\",\"planets\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"There are more stars in the observable universe than grains of sand on every beach on Earth, and the space between them is still stretching.\",\"A day on the International Space Station is 90 minutes long, because that is how long it takes to go round the Earth once.\"]}]}],[\"music\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"music\",\"song\",\"songs\",\"melody\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"The shiver down your spine at a good bit of music comes before the moment you expect, not on it: the brain is rewarding itself for predicting what comes next.\",\"Music uses the same reward circuits as food and friends, which is why a song can lift a mood in seconds and a smell cannot.\"]}]}],[\"money\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"money\",\"cash\",\"banknotes\",\"coins\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Most money is not paper: only a small fraction of what is counted as money exists as notes and coins, and the rest is numbers in accounts.\",\"Notes are printed on cotton and linen, not wood pulp, which is why a note survives the wash better than a receipt does.\"]}]}],[\"beetles\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"beetle\",\"beetles\",\"insect\",\"insects\",\"bug\",\"bugs\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"One in four of every animal species that has ever been named is a beetle - about 400,000 of them - so a beetle is the safest guess for any unnamed insect.\",\"Insects breathe through holes in their sides instead of lungs, which is part of why there are no insects the size of a cat.\"]}]}],[\"dinosaurs\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"dinosaur\",\"dinosaurs\",\"t rex\",\"t-rex\",\"tyrannosaurus\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Birds are dinosaurs: the line that survived the asteroid is the one that became birds, which is why a chicken's skeleton is closer to a T. rex than a lizard's is.\",\"Many dinosaurs were feathered and coloured, not scaly and green: the skin we have fossil evidence for on several of them is a coat of feathers.\"]}]}],[\"mountains\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"mountain\",\"mountains\",\"everest\",\"himalayas\",\"alps\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Everest is the highest, not the tallest: from its base on the sea floor, Mauna Kea in Hawaii is over ten kilometres tall.\",\"Everest is still going up by a few millimetres a year as India pushes into Asia, and the summit is a marine limestone - it was sea floor once.\"]}]}],[\"water\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"water\",\"ice\",\"snow\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Water is the only common substance that is lighter as a solid, which is why ice floats and a pond freezes from the top down instead of from the bottom.\",\"Hot water can freeze faster than cold in some conditions - it has a name, the Mpemba effect - and nobody has a settled explanation for it.\"]}]}],[\"octopus\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"octopus\",\"octopuses\",\"octopi\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"An octopus can change colour and the texture of its skin in under a second, and it is colour-blind - nobody knows for certain how it matches colours it cannot see.\",\"Two thirds of an octopus's neurons are in its arms, so an arm can taste what it touches and work on its own while the head does something else.\"]}]}],[\"bananas\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"banana\",\"bananas\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"The banana plant is not a tree: it is the largest herb, and what looks like a trunk is the bases of the leaves packed together.\",\"A banana is slightly radioactive because it is rich in potassium, and so is a potato - the dose from either is far too small to matter.\"]}]}],[\"body\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"body\",\"bodies\",\"human body\",\"the body\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Your body makes about a litre of new bone a year of the two or so kilograms it carries, which is why a broken bone heals back stronger at the break.\",\"You are taller in the morning: the discs between your vertebrae squash flat over a day and spring back overnight, up to a centimetre and a half.\"]}]}],[\"chilli\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chilli\",\"chilli pepper\",\"chillies\",\"chili\",\"chilies\",\"jalapeno\",\"jalapenos\",\"hot sauce\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"Chilli heat is not a taste: capsaicin trips the receptor that senses a hot pan, which is why your mouth reads it as burning and why milk works where water does not.\",\"The hottest chillies are measured in Scoville units, and a habanero can be a hundred times hotter than a jalapeno that looks the same size.\"]}]}]]}")?;
